        "aiSupplement": {
          "explanation": [
            {
              "text": "In dehydration the OH group and an H atom on a neighbouring carbon are removed as H<sub>2</sub>O, and the C=C bond forms between those two carbons. In hexan-2-ol, CH<sub>3</sub>CH(OH)CH<sub>2</sub>CH<sub>2</sub>CH<sub>2</sub>CH<sub>3</sub>, the OH is on C2, so the H can come from C1 or C3.",
              "refs": [
                "syllabus:16.1(2)",
                "syllabus:14.2(1)"
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "Losing H from C1 gives hex-1-ene. Losing H from C3 gives hex-2-ene, which exists as cis and trans isomers, and both can form. The double bond can never be between C3 and C4, so hex-3-ene (cis or trans) cannot form.",
              "refs": [
                "syllabus:13.4(3)"
              ]
            }
          ],
          "optionAnalysis": [
            {
              "key": "A",
              "correct": false,
              "text": "Trans-hex-3-ene needs a C3=C4 double bond, but the OH group is on C2, so the double bond must involve C2."
            },
            {
              "key": "B",
              "correct": true,
              "text": "H removed from C1 gives hex-1-ene; H removed from C3 gives hex-2-ene, including the cis isomer."
            },
            {
              "key": "C",
              "correct": false,
              "text": "Misses hex-2-ene, which forms when H is removed from C3 rather than C1."
            },
            {
              "key": "D",
              "correct": false,
              "text": "Misses hex-1-ene, which forms when H is removed from the terminal CH<sub>3</sub> (C1)."
            }
          ],
          "reasoningChain": [
            "Hexan-2-ol: OH on C2; neighbouring carbons are C1 and C3.",
            "C1–C2 double bond: hex-1-ene (1 can form).",
            "C2–C3 double bond: cis- and trans-hex-2-ene (2 can form).",
            "No route to a C3=C4 double bond (3 cannot form).",
            "1 and 2 only: option B."
          ],
          "inferredMistakes": [
